BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 657 Td (separately when the requirements command succeeds.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58 644 Td (5. Prepare the database) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 622 Td (Django migrations create or update the database tables needed by the application. From the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 609 Td (folder as manage.py, run:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 76 596 Td (python manage.py migrate) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 583 Td (The project uses SQLite, configured in quiz_project/settings.py. The database is the db.sqlite3) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 570 Td (file in the project folder. Migrations create the Django user and session tables and the quiz) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 557 Td (score table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 544 Td (If you are starting fresh, migrate creates the database schema. If db.sqlite3 already exists,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 531 Td (migrations bring its schema up to date; they do not normally erase existing user or score data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 518 Td (Keep a backup before moving or replacing a database file.) Tj ET
