BT /F2 12 Tf 58 479 Td (6. How the website is organized) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 457 Td (A browser requests a URL. Django matches that URL to a view. The view handles any required logic,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 444 Td (such as checking a login or calculating a score, then renders an HTML template. The browser) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 431 Td (receives the page and applies the project CSS and JavaScript.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 418 Td (The main routes are /login/ for signing in, /logout/ for signing out, /register/ for account) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 405 Td (creation, and /quiz/ for the quiz. The root path / requires login and redirects a signed-in user) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 392 Td (to the quiz. A person who is not signed in is sent to the login page.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 379 Td (Django middleware enables sessions and authentication. The session remembers that the user is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 366 Td (signed in and also stores the quiz deadline. HTML forms include CSRF tokens, a Django protection) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 353 Td (against forged form submissions.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58 340 Td (7. Registration and login) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 318 Td (The registration form asks for a username and password. The password must have at least eight) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 305 Td (characters. When saving a new account, the form calls Django's set_password method, which hashes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 292 Td (the password instead of storing the original password as readable text.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 279 Td (After registration, the user is signed in automatically and redirected to the quiz. Existing users) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 266 Td (sign in through Django's built-in LoginView. The logout button submits a POST request to Django's) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 253 Td (built-in LogoutView.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58 240 Td (8. Quiz, timer, and scoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 218 Td (The five Python questions and their answer options are defined in quiz/views.py. On a quiz page) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 205 Td (request, the view sends the questions and remaining time to quiz/templates/quiz.html. Each) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 192 Td (question uses radio buttons so the student chooses one answer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 179 Td (On the first quiz page request, the server stores a deadline five minutes in the future in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 166 Td (user session. Refreshing the page uses the existing deadline, so it does not restart the full five) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 153 Td (minutes. JavaScript updates the visible countdown every second and submits the form when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 140 Td (countdown reaches zero.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 127 Td (When Django receives the submitted form, it compares each submitted answer with the correct answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 114 Td (and adds one point for each match. The score is out of five. A score of 4 or 5 gets the excellent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 101 Td (message, 2 or 3 gets the keep-practising message, and 0 or 1 gets the try-again message.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 88 Td (If the server-side deadline has passed, the result says time is up. The app still computes a score) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 58 75 Td (from the answers received with the submission. The result page shows the current score and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 270 24 Td (Page 2) Tj ET
